# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context filter.
#
# Every image builds from the REPOSITORY ROOT, because the npm workspace lock
# file lives at the root. A small context makes the build fast and it keeps a
# secret out of an image layer.
#
# Docker reads only this file at the context root. A rule that starts with `!`
# adds a path back after a wider rule removed it. Order matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# `npm ci` installs inside the image. A host node_modules directory holds
# binaries that were built for Windows and they would break a Linux image.
**/node_modules

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env MUST NOT enter an image. Compose passes the values as environment
# variables at run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# The image builds its own output. A stale host copy would hide a real fault.
web/dist
web/.vite
**/.vite
contracts/artifacts
contracts/cache
contracts/coverage
contracts/typechain-types
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output

# --- Legacy directories ----------------------------------------------------
# The Truffle and Ganache stack was replaced by contracts/ and web/. Do not
# copy it into an image.
backend
frontend

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation never changes an image. Excluding it keeps the build cache
# valid when only a document changes.
*.md
docs
LICENSE

# --- Editor and operating system ------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.editorconfig

# --- Local tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
Makefile
compose.yaml
compose.override.yaml
compose.prod.yaml
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.cache
tmp
temp

# --- Test and CI artifacts -------------------------------------------------
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# --- Keep what the images need --------------------------------------------
# The Dockerfiles copy these paths, so add them back after the wide rules.
!docker
!scripts/rpc.mjs
